  "configuration_id": "config_018",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows RNA multiprofile with PCA and avgpool is the strongest setting (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), outperforming single-profile RNA, transformer aggregation, and scGPT avgpool; image-only ResNet50 is weak (0.208), leaving uncertainty whether image features can add complementary signal. config_018 keeps the best RNA profile/aggregation and adds the already-tested ResNet50 image encoder with a simple concat fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion improves over the best RNA-only baseline. It is the best next budget use because it exploits the strongest RNA evidence while probing the central multimodal/fusion question with minimal additional confounds, using a simple fusion baseline before trying weighted fusion or stronger image encoders."
